reading (honest):
- Jain on END TOTALS passes before AND after the fix (0.998 vs 0.999-1.0): it cannot see the pile-up. The new peak-concurrency field does: pre-fix every agent ran >1 task at once (max 3); post-fix max 1-2 with 0-1 agents above 1.
- post-fix peak 2 is expected here: 16 concurrent submitters > 5 agents, so when all 5 are busy the least-loaded one takes a second lease. There is NO per-agent concurrency cap in server.py (design observation for R-178, not changed in this batch).
- latencies are co-located (SUT + generator + storage on 2 vCPU) and not comparable to any target; criteria stay proposed; L0 proves no capacity level.
